{% extends "base.html.j2" %}
{% block title %}Backtest | ISDS Thematic Watcher{% endblock %}
{% block description %}A small exploratory backtest of the deterministic scorer, reported in three separate buckets &mdash; in-sample seed recovery, the out-of-sample holdout that carries the headline metric, and the live prospective digest archive &mdash; so the seeds never inflate the headline.{% endblock %}

{% block content %}
<section class="page-head">
  <div class="measure">
    <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <ol>
        <li><a href="{{ root }}index.html">Home</a></li>
        <li aria-current="page">Backtest</li>
      </ol>
    </nav>
    <p class="page-kicker">Scorer evaluation</p>
    <h1 class="page-title">Historical backtest</h1>
    <p class="page-lede">
      A small exploratory backtest on known cases &mdash; not a comprehensive validation.
      It scores familiar investor&ndash;State cases with the same deterministic keyword scorer
      the pipeline uses, at the same digest threshold ({{ bt.threshold }}), and reports the results
      in <strong>three separate buckets</strong> so the cases that trained the fingerprint never
      inflate the headline.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band">
  <div class="measure">
    <h2 class="section-head">Why three buckets</h2>
    <div class="doc-body">
      <p>
        An earlier version of this page folded every case into one blended confusion matrix. That
        flattered the scorer: the development <em>seed</em> awards are the very cases whose vocabulary
        <em>defines</em> the fingerprint, so recovering them proves only that the system recognises
        what generated it &mdash; circular, not predictive. To keep the headline honest, the cases are
        split into three clearly-labelled buckets, each reported on its own:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Seed recovery</strong> &mdash; the three development seed awards, scored
          <em>in-sample</em>. A sanity check that the fingerprint recognises its own source material.
          Its numbers never enter any headline.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Out-of-sample holdout</strong> &mdash; four held-out positives and clear off-theme
          negatives, none of them used in development. This bucket carries the descriptive
          out-of-sample record: a confusion matrix over twenty items with four positives. It is
          too small to support derived performance rates, and none are reported.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Live prospective</strong> &mdash; the live weekly digest archive, the only test
          that scores cases the system has never seen before the outcome is known. Reported as an
          honest status, not as numbers from this corpus.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Every case&rsquo;s text comes from material already in the repository &mdash; the seeds from
        their verbatim seed-tagged phrases in <code>fingerprint.yaml</code>, the holdout items
        verbatim from <code>holdout_set.json</code>. Nothing here is fabricated, and any case whose
        text could not be resolved in-repo was excluded rather than invented.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band band-alt">
  <div class="measure">
    <p class="page-kicker">Bucket 1 &mdash; in-sample</p>
    <h2 class="section-head">Seed recovery</h2>
    <p class="page-lede" style="font-size:16.5px; margin:0 0 22px;">
      The three development seed awards, scored against the lexicon their own text defines. This is a
      recovery check, <strong>not predictive evidence</strong> &mdash; these numbers are deliberately
      kept out of every headline.
    </p>
    <div class="doc-body">
      <p>
        Seeds recovered at the digest threshold ({{ bt.threshold }}):
        <strong>{{ bt.seed.recovered }} of {{ bt.seed.total }}</strong>. Because the seeds trained the
        fingerprint, a perfect recovery here is the expected, uninformative result &mdash; a failure
        would signal a bug, but a pass says nothing about field performance.
      </p>
      <table>
        <caption class="visually-hidden">
          In-sample seed recovery: each seed award, the score the deterministic scorer assigned, and
          the predicted band.
        </caption>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col">Seed award</th>
            <th scope="col">Score</th>
            <th scope="col">Predicted band</th>
            <th scope="col">Recovered</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {% for c in bt.seed.cases %}
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">{{ c.name }}</th>
            <td>{{ c.score }}</td>
            <td><span class="badge badge-{{ c.band | band_class }}">{{ c.band }}</span></td>
            <td>{{ 'yes' if c.pred == 1 else 'no' }}</td>
          </tr>
          {% endfor %}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band">
  <div class="measure">
    <p class="page-kicker">Bucket 2 &mdash; out-of-sample (the headline)</p>
    <h2 class="section-head">Out-of-sample holdout</h2>
    <p class="page-lede" style="font-size:16.5px; margin:0 0 22px;">
      Four held-out positives (Loewen, Mondev, Apotex, Philip&nbsp;Morris v.&nbsp;Uruguay) and clear
      off-theme negatives &mdash; {{ bt.holdout.total }} cases in all, none used in development. The
      record below is descriptive and is computed on this bucket <strong>alone</strong>; the seeds
      are not in it. Four positives cannot support a headline performance figure.
    </p>
    <div class="doc-body">
      <table>
        <caption class="visually-hidden">
          Confusion matrix of predicted match versus true label across {{ bt.holdout.total }}
          out-of-sample cases.
        </caption>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col"></th>
            <th scope="col">Predicted match (&#8805;&nbsp;{{ bt.threshold }})</th>
            <th scope="col">Predicted pass (&lt;&nbsp;{{ bt.threshold }})</th>
            <th scope="col">Row total</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">On-theme (label&nbsp;=&nbsp;1)</th>
            <td><strong>TP {{ bt.holdout.tp }}</strong></td>
            <td>FN {{ bt.holdout.fn }}</td>
            <td>{{ bt.holdout.n_pos }}</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">Off-theme (label&nbsp;=&nbsp;0)</th>
            <td>FP {{ bt.holdout.fp }}</td>
            <td><strong>TN {{ bt.holdout.tn }}</strong></td>
            <td>{{ bt.holdout.n_neg }}</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <p>
        Three of the four labelled positives cleared the deterministic threshold of
        40 &mdash; exact Clopper&ndash;Pearson 95% confidence interval 0.19 to 0.99.
        All sixteen negatives scored zero, so this set contains no boundary case and
        cannot measure precision. Derived rates (precision, recall, accuracy, F1) are
        not reported here: over twenty items with four positives they are arithmetic,
        not performance. The production pipeline publishes at a floor of 25, not at
        this threshold, and no item has reached 40 in 347 screenings.
      </p>
      <p>
        On this out-of-sample set the scorer makes
        {{ bt.holdout.fp + bt.holdout.fn }} miss{{ 'es' if (bt.holdout.fp + bt.holdout.fn) != 1 else '' }}:
        {{ bt.holdout.fn }} false negative{{ 's' if bt.holdout.fn != 1 else '' }} and
        {{ bt.holdout.fp }} false positive{{ 's' if bt.holdout.fp != 1 else '' }}. The misses are
        listed in full below &mdash; the point of a backtest is the failures, not the passes.
      </p>

      <h3>Per-case results</h3>
      <table>
        <caption class="visually-hidden">
          Per-case out-of-sample results: case, group, label, score, predicted band, and miss note.
        </caption>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col">Case</th>
            <th scope="col">Group</th>
            <th scope="col">Label</th>
            <th scope="col">Score</th>
            <th scope="col">Predicted band</th>
            <th scope="col">Note</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {% for c in bt.holdout.cases %}
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">{{ c.name }}</th>
            <td>{{ c.group }}</td>
            <td>{{ 'on-theme' if c.label == 1 else 'off-theme' }}</td>
            <td>{{ c.score }}</td>
            <td>
              <span class="badge badge-{{ c.band | band_class }}">{{ c.band }}</span>
            </td>
            <td>
              {% if c.correct %}correct{% else %}<strong>{{ c.miss_kind }}</strong>{% endif %}
            </td>
          </tr>
          {% endfor %}
        </tbody>
      </table>

      {% if bt.holdout.false_negatives or bt.holdout.false_positives %}
      <h3>Where it misses, and why</h3>
      {% if bt.holdout.false_negatives %}
      <h4>False negatives</h4>
      <ul>
        {% for c in bt.holdout.false_negatives %}
        <li><strong>{{ c.name }}</strong> (score {{ c.score }}). {{ c.reason }}</li>
        {% endfor %}
      </ul>
      {% endif %}
      {% if bt.holdout.false_positives %}
      <h4>False positives</h4>
      <ul>
        {% for c in bt.holdout.false_positives %}
        <li><strong>{{ c.name }}</strong> (score {{ c.score }}). {{ c.reason }}</li>
        {% endfor %}
      </ul>
      {% endif %}
      {% endif %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band band-alt">
  <div class="measure">
    <p class="page-kicker">Bucket 3 &mdash; live prospective</p>
    <h2 class="section-head">Live prospective</h2>
    <p class="page-lede" style="font-size:16.5px; margin:0 0 22px;">
      Status: <strong>{{ bt.live.status }}</strong>
    </p>
    <div class="doc-body">
      <p>{{ bt.live.detail }}</p>
    </div>
    <p class="archive-foot">
      See the <a href="{{ root }}digests/index.html">digest archive</a> for the live record, and the
      <a href="{{ root }}methodology.html">methodology</a> for how the scorer and its threshold are defined.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
{% endblock %}
